      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ba749f34dca6b351d658330|full_name}: This is the real issue. SDK3 is not complete yet, support for SDK2 shouldn't be fully dropped until SDK3 is complete. Why not simply add the constraints to the whitelist on SDK2? This is a very simple thing that should take almost no time to do.\nCurrently the only way to do anything like constraints using SDK2 is to use hacky workarounds like rigid bodies, autocam script, etc. Even still there are some things which aren't possible without the constraints. Seems a bit ridiculous to not spend 5 minutes to add these components to the whitelist.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
